      "title": "Search term interpolated into SQL",
      "description": "The index action puts params[:q] straight into the SQL text of the where clause. Any authenticated user controls that text. An authenticated caller can inject SQL and read or change any row, including api_token and admin columns. Pass the search term as a bound parameter and escape LIKE wildcards with sanitize_sql_like.",
      "suggested_change": "    users = users.where(\"email LIKE ?\", \"%#{User.sanitize_sql_like(params[:q])}%\") if params[:q].present?",
      "source": "semgrep:ruby.rails.security.injection.tainted-sql-string.tainted-sql-string",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "The index action puts params[:q] straight into the SQL text of the where clause. Any authenticated user controls that text.",
      "consequence": "An authenticated caller can inject SQL and read or change any row, including api_token and admin columns.",
      "fix": "Pass the search term as a bound parameter and escape LIKE wildcards with sanitize_sql_like."
    },
